      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-12T21:57:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about renaming this to ufshcd_keyslot_valid(), then adding a function likewise for validating the cap_idx:\n\n static bool ufshcd_cap_idx_valid(struct ufs_hba *hba, unsigned int cap_idx)\n {\n        return cap_idx \u003c hba-\u003ecrypto_capabilities.num_crypto_cap;\n }\n\nThen the callers look like:\n\n        if (!ufshcd_is_crypto_enabled(hba) ||\n            !ufshcd_cap_idx_valid(hba, cap_idx) ||\n            !ufshcd_keyslot_valid(hba, slot))\n                return -EINVAL;\n\nI think that\u0027s much easier to understand.  Also it avoids the issue of creating a function with external linkage that\u0027s not in the \"ufshcd_\" \"namespace\".",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "a00871734c25f3fb0e9543565e88ded74a489ca2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
