    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5c5e5e56_cd2bf6b1",
        "filename": "drivers/scsi/ufs/ufshcd-crypto.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 116,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-16T23:48:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also, wouldn\u0027t wmb() be sufficient, since this code is only writing to the hardware, not reading?  Why mb()?\n\nAlso take a look at Section 7.1.3 \"CRYPTOCFG Configuration Procedure\" in the UFSHCI v2.1 standard.  It makes recommendations different from what is done here.  Basically:\n\n- If CFGE is set before, clear it before writing the key\n- Write the key before setting CFGE\n- Only write up to dword 16 (the one containing CFGE), not 31\n\nIt also says the key must be written \"sequentially\", so given that and the fact that it documents the ordering w.r.t. CFGE, perhaps wmb() is even needed after every dword written?",
      "parentUuid": "91a386de_66026a47",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 116,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 116,
        "endChar": 6
      },
